link_hdmi_frl.c, above `static int frl_restart_backoff_ms;`:
Test knobs (cinemaONE, 2026-09-27), for dc_hpo_frl_retrain_in_place=2 only.
Through the VRROOM a restart was asked for again ~0.4 s after the one before
(LTP 5,6,7,8 every time), up to 17 times before it settled.
  dc_hpo_frl_restart_backoff_ms: after a restart, leave a new FLT_Update
    unserved (and set) for this long; 0 = serve at once
  dc_hpo_frl_force_restart: write 1 and the next poll round restarts the
    streams once, as if asked (for timing page flips across a restart)
Every restart is logged at KERN_INFO, whatever drm.debug says.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_hdmi_frl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_hdmi_frl.c
